<title>USA: Florida governor says no deal on tobacco rise.</title>
<headline>Florida governor says no deal on tobacco rise.</headline>
<dateline>TALLAHASSEE, Fla. 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Florida's governor on Tuesday ruled out scuttling a 1994 law the state is using to sue the tobacco industry to win legislative support for a 10 cent cigarette tax increase he wants.</p>
<p>Speaking to reporters to kick off an anti-smoking advertising campaign, Democrat Gov. Lawton Chiles said he remains optimistic his cigarette tax proposal will win legislative approval.</p>
<p>Opposition to the tax from Republican leaders in both legislative chambers was formidable, he said.</p>
